WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.530
The AI Work You Should Not Automate. Automation is valuable

2
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:09.060
when it removes repetitive friction. It becomes risky when it

3
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.591
hides a decision that deserves a person’s name. Do not

4
00:00:13.591 --> 00:00:18.121
automate publication, payments, access changes, sensitive communication, legal or financial

5
00:00:18.121 --> 00:00:22.651
interpretation, or any decision that cannot be reversed cleanly. Use

6
00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:27.181
assistance to prepare the record; keep authority with the person

7
00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:31.711
accountable for the outcome. Drafting is not deciding. Let the

8
00:00:31.711 --> 00:00:36.241
tool create a first pass, identify missing evidence, or organize

9
00:00:36.241 --> 00:00:40.772
alternatives. A human still decides what the organization will say

10
00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:45.302
or do. Classification is not permission. A system can label

11
00:00:45.302 --> 00:00:49.832
a request. That does not mean it should approve access,

12
00:00:49.832 --> 00:00:54.362
trigger a payment, or make a commitment. Speed is not

13
00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:58.892
the objective. The right pace is the one that preserves

14
00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:03.423
judgment, gives people time to review, and leaves a usable

15
00:01:03.423 --> 00:01:07.953
trail for the next person who inherits the work. Use

16
00:01:07.953 --> 00:01:12.483
the Five Questions when a workflow starts asking for more

17
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:12.936
authority.
